              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a kingdom, then the Telugu for to reign over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: తొలుత",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తొలుత — toluta — \"at first\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తొలుత నాకు భయం వేసింది. toluta nāku bhayaṁ vēsindi. At first I felt afraid."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A storytelling word, a little formal; in speech మొదట says the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తొలుత (toluta) is native Dravidian, built on toli, \"beginning; first, former\", which DEDR 3516 lists with Tamil tol, \"old, ancient\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
