          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అనంతరం — anantaraṁ — \"afterwards; after that\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "భోజనం అనంతరం అందరూ ఇంటికి వెళ్ళారు. bhōjanaṁ anantaraṁ andarū iṇṭiki veḷḷāru. After the meal everyone went home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It follows a noun as తరువాత does, but sounds more formal: news readers use it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అనంతరం (anantaraṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit anantaram, \"immediately after\", from an-antara, \"having no interval\" (CDIAL 287)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
