          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరుసటి రోజు — marusaṭi rōju — \"the next day\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరుసటి రోజు అతను మళ్ళీ వచ్చాడు. marusaṭi rōju atanu maḷḷī vaccāḍu. The next day he came again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరుసటి works with other time words too: మరుసటి వారం, the next week."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మరుసటి రోజు (marusaṭi rōju) is a Telugu phrase: marusaṭi, \"the following\", is native Dravidian (DEDR 4766, beside Tamil maṟu, \"other, next\"), and rōju is the everyday word for a day."
            }
          ]
        },
